    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                "word": "alphabetism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ee69c81d-3ade-4a4d-ae9b-a4f1c8754213",
                        "entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "alphabetisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0929c8c2-e1db-3467-bead-2054e5a1d81b",
                        "entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An initialism: an abbreviation which is read letter by letter, such as UN."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af075ef5-a966-46aa-a1ec-a0a8a81feed7",
                                "sense_id": "0929c8c2-e1db-3467-bead-2054e5a1d81b",
                                "text": "Some alphabetisms are written as if they weren't alphabetisms at all, like deejay for DJ, disc jockey, or emcee for MC, master of ceremonies."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0cd6da50-7080-3d4c-a599-4b7f88cbec5b",
                        "entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The ability to read an alphabet, a rudimentary form of literacy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "991a98e8-2a8c-465e-8a4a-5caadc561d19",
                                "sense_id": "0cd6da50-7080-3d4c-a599-4b7f88cbec5b",
                                "text": "Some of the activities involved in ... corvée and military needs stimulated the spread of a certain type of minimal alphabetism for inventorying and most likely encouraged the development of a professional scribalism for record-keeping and book-keeping."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bba614b5-dc31-362d-ba8c-21c6254e908e",
                        "entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Excessive reliance upon the alphabet or alphabetic structures."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5069412a-cfb2-4c50-9e22-638f0f04b4b4",
                                "sense_id": "bba614b5-dc31-362d-ba8c-21c6254e908e",
                                "text": "The answer, I suggest, is that phonemism is rooted in alphabetism. Indeed, many linguists have suggested that there really is a /g/ phoneme at the end of 'fang' and other [ŋ]-final words in English, except that they are not pronounced!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "657c5cb7-ccff-3da5-98f8-565952ae503e",
                        "entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Discrimination on the basis of the first letter of a name."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db0c6e20-2892-470d-a97c-c870437ca459",
                                "sense_id": "657c5cb7-ccff-3da5-98f8-565952ae503e",
                                "text": "The injustice of \"alphabetism\" is, of course, a thorn in the Zitser side, and he playfully promises to assign the problem to \"alphabetically neutral\" aides."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c43064a-9f08-431f-bf4f-5bdcd61915b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "source_sense_description": "form of literacy",
                        "target_lang_word": "Alphabetismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Alphabetismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2703456f-3746-36ed-a90f-cfb2c7eb4983",
                                        "entry_id": "a8dbf96b-8c81-36b4-9122-6c681b1072b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fähigkeit, lesen (und meist auch schreiben) zu können"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "no-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cab35210-b31f-44e1-ad50-637d33e8c0a9",
                                                "sense_id": "2703456f-3746-36ed-a90f-cfb2c7eb4983",
                                                "text": "Der Alphabetismus wird in Deutschland heutzutage vorausgesetzt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a113e205-04ae-494f-873f-d73e6052d6cc",
                                                "sense_id": "2703456f-3746-36ed-a90f-cfb2c7eb4983",
                                                "text": "„Der hier dargestellten Indikator \"Alphabetismus\" weist auf ihre unterpriviligierte Stellung in vielen Bereichen des innerfamiliären und gesellschaftlichen Lebens hin, in der heute eine wesentliche Ursache für Unterentwicklung gesehen wird.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57590c47-082c-4917-96f1-f69442a5a150",
                                                "sense_id": "2703456f-3746-36ed-a90f-cfb2c7eb4983",
                                                "text": "„Es sei an dieser Stelle noch einmal erwähnt, dass sich die, in Tabelle 1 angezeigten Werte auf den funktionalen Alphabetismus (2.3) beziehen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73bc1eaa-46d1-303a-84d7-802c8608054f",
                                        "entry_id": "a8dbf96b-8c81-36b4-9122-6c681b1072b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Reihe von meist Anfangsbuchstaben mehrerer Wörter, die eine Abkürzung des Gesamtbegriffes darstellen und Buchstabe für Buchstabe gelesen/gesprochen werden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Sprachwissenschaft"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63972909-73f4-48e9-8d66-442e97dc2ccb",
                                                "sense_id": "73bc1eaa-46d1-303a-84d7-802c8608054f",
                                                "text": "CDU oder SPD sind Alphabetismen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8e93413-f45c-4ac9-a550-659ec34f78cc",
                                                "sense_id": "73bc1eaa-46d1-303a-84d7-802c8608054f",
                                                "text": "„Viele Alphabetismen sind in der Alltagssprache anzutreffen, vor allem die neuen Medien betreffend (TV, CD, LP, PC, VIP, USA, OED).“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd4138bc-85bf-4478-a1ab-e660df45d7a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "2841b017-da15-3166-b2ae-c6189f53c87d",
                        "source_sense_description": "form of discrimination",
                        "target_lang_word": "alphabétisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alphabétisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dd8cc5f-6ddd-32ae-8b30-41292e3aafa1",
                                        "entry_id": "95af0866-e72e-3732-ac72-a2d077a49616",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fait, pour un système d’écriture notant la parole, d’utiliser un alphabet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7c248c8-5e94-40bf-b9ac-a6d6b44c586e",
                                                "sense_id": "6dd8cc5f-6ddd-32ae-8b30-41292e3aafa1",
                                                "text": "L’alphabétisme crée l’écriture segmentale : tandis que les syllabaires regroupent plusieurs sons sous un seul symbole, les alphabets attribuent des sons individuels à des symboles ; le degré suivant, observable dans certaines écritures plus récentes comme le hangul, associe des traits phonologiques individuels à des caractéristiques graphiques des symboles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95bbcd3c-1de2-3801-af18-375eee939314",
                                        "entry_id": "95af0866-e72e-3732-ac72-a2d077a49616",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Résultat d’une alphabétisation réussie : capacité à lire et à écrire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UNESCO"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2dbb102-4b69-4f72-b87a-5d9adc67d72c",
                                                "sense_id": "95bbcd3c-1de2-3801-af18-375eee939314",
                                                "text": "Le programme d’alphabétisme fonctionnel vise les jeunes de 15 ans au plus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b4a67aa-3512-49cc-a6cd-0426548626b7",
                                                "sense_id": "95bbcd3c-1de2-3801-af18-375eee939314",
                                                "text": "Le nombre d’analphabètes est passé de 871 millions au cours de la période 1985-1994 à 774 millions pour la période suivante (2000-2006), ce qui a fait passer le taux mondial d’alphabétisation des adultes de 76% à 83,6%."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
